{"id":"DOC-071","doc_kind":"other","title":"EN-AR terminology glossary — the canonical bilingual terms `NFR-039` names (`src/Acmp.Web/src/i18n/glossary.json`)","lifecycle_status":"Draft","custom_attributes":"{\"path\": \"src/Acmp.Web/src/i18n/glossary.json\", \"built_by\": \"WBS-40.1 / DW-069 step (a), DEC-167 q1. PR #392 -> squash 25c96733; merge-commit runs CI 34477817666 and Security 34477817797 success.\", \"location_note\": \"The SECOND narrative artefact outside docs/ (DOC-070 was the first), and the first that is machine-readable: it sits beside the two locale bundles it governs so the CI term check can read it directly. One file, no mirror (DEC-167 q1 declined both the tamheed-package/docs/ home and a generated markdown mirror). The three former claimants - docs/README.md section G, docs/governance/glossary.md and design-handoff/claude-design-input-package.md line 113 - now point HERE, and this file points nowhere (LL-010: the circular pointer is closed).\", \"content_state_2026_09_10\": \"24 terms: DOC-049's 22 plus Architecture -> الهيكلة (DEC-032) and Secretary of the Committee -> أمين سر اللجنة (design package line 20). ONLY those two carry an Arabic value (status canonical); the other 22 are status proposed with ar null, because every Arabic value is the operator's ruling (DEC-156 d3) and an agent never fills one in from ar.json, which is the artefact the glossary is checked against. allowedVariants is empty until the rulings land. Hence lifecycle Draft: the artefact exists and is the single source; its content is not yet ruled.\", \"the_slate\": \"tamheed-package/docs/i18n-term-slate.md, generated by scripts/gen-i18n-term-slate.mjs (DEC-165 n4 shape, DEC-167 q3 medium): section A = the 24 terms with every surface and rendering, section B = the 64 other short labels with more than one rendering, 88 Ruling: lines. Census 1,976 keys paired / 1,098 short labels / 77 multi-rendering, identical to DEC-156 d2. Regeneration over unchanged inputs is byte-identical.\", \"what_is_NOT_done\": \"DW-069 step (b) - the operator's rulings - and step (c) - scripts/check-i18n-terms.mjs wired into ci.yml's frontend job. The check waits by DEC-156 d2 and DEC-110 d6: it cannot pass until the allowlist is authored, and a red gate on main is forbidden. No acceptance criterion for NFR-039 exists or may be written (DW-069, trap 16c).\", \"related\": \"NFR-039, DW-069, DW-076, WBS-40.1, WBS-40.2, DOC-049, DEC-032, DEC-156, DEC-165 n4, DEC-167, LL-010, PR #392.\"}","last_referenced":"2026-09-10T12:51:56Z"}
